  "status_text": "A search is being answered case by case, in public. The question: can a circuit of at most 11, or at most 12, AND, OR and NOT gates, each reading at most two wires, decide whether a three-by-three grid of links contains a perfect matching? We cut it into 332 cases by the two gates such a circuit opens with and put them on the desk. By 18:18 UTC the crowd had finished 194, each checked in Lean, and every one came back the same: no such circuit starts that way. At 11 gates, 116 of 166 cases were done. Both questions were still open at that time (L-meta-17389, L-meta-17388).",
